This file documents third-party material incorporated into `rand_philox`.

================================================================================
src/philox.rs — Philox4x32-10 constants and known-answer vectors
================================================================================

The Philox round multiplier/key-bump constants and the three known-answer
vectors used to freeze the algorithm are taken from Random123, the counter-based
RNG library of D. E. Shaw Research:

    Salmon, J. K., Moraes, M. A., Dror, R. O., & Shaw, D. E. (2011).
    "Parallel Random Numbers: As Easy as 1, 2, 3." Proc. SC'11.
    https://www.deshawresearch.com/resources_random123.html

The `philox4x32_10` block function here is an independent Rust implementation;
only the published constants and test vectors are reused. Random123 is
